                <pb facs="0090" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v23/pg57"/>

                <head>42. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="1" xml:id="d42-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-11-10">November 10,
                        1960</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Minutes of Special Group Meeting, 10 November 1960</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PRESENT</label>
                    <item>Messrs. Merchant, Douglas, Gray, Dulles, Bissell</item>
                </list>
                <p>[Omitted here is discussion of other subjects.]</p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">7. Contingency Plans for the Congo</p>
                <p>Mr. Bissell mentioned briefly that we are making certain contingency plans for
                    the Congo against the possibility of a pro-Soviet Lumumba government, or
                    complications arising from a militant Katanga independence movement.</p>
                <p>Mr. Scott, who had replaced Mr. Merchant in the meeting, said that the African
                    Bureau of State agrees with CIA’s general method of proceeding with these
                    plans.</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">1 paragraph (11 lines) not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>TA Parrott</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
